  "notes": "After ruffing the opening heart lead, South's main concern is to play the trump suit for only one loser. The ♠K and ♠Q will always provide at least one trick for the defenders. South must play the suit to maximize the chance for only 1 loser.\n\nSouth should cross to the dummy in diamonds (crossing in clubs is more likely to lead to a defensive ruff) and finesse in spades. On the above lie of the cards, South will immediately succeed. It would have done East no good to split his honours when North led a spade.\n\nIf the first spade finesse loses, South should ruff the heart return, cross to dummy again, this time in clubs, and take a second finesse in spades. If this finesse wins, South can draw the last trump with the ♠A and easily take the balance of the tricks.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
    "After ruffing the opening heart lead, South's main concern is to play the trump suit for only one loser. The ♠K and ♠Q will always provide at least one trick for the defenders. South must play the suit to maximize the chance for only 1 loser.",
